  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contribution to universal access of DR Congo populations to effective interventions to fight malaria - Congo (Democratic Republic) (01-Jan-2015-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Congo (Democratic Republic), Malaria, Population Services International (PSI HQ)This program has the following goals: Contribute to the improvement of health status of the population of DRC by reducing human and socio-economic burden caused by malaria. The objectives of this program are: Bring at least 80% of people at risk of malaria to sleep under an LLIN.  Confirm at least 80% of suspected malaria cases seen in the public healht facilities and in the community by micrroscopy or RDTs in 308 targeted HZs.  Cover at least 80% of pregnant women attending ANC with IPTp according to national guidelines in targeted 308 targetd HZs.  Treat all confirmed malaria cases according to national guidelines in public health facilities and community in 308 targeted HZs</narrative>
  </description>
